<title>SWITZERLAND: ALPINE SKIING-RIEGLER WINS WOMEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-RIEGLER WINS WOMEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>LAAX, Switzerland 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Claudia Riegler of  New Zealand won a women's World Cup slalom on Sunday in a time of one minute 20.75 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Italy's Lara Magoni finished second in 1:20.82 and third place was shared by Pernilla Wiberg of Sweden and Switzerland's Martina Accola with 1:20.83.  </p>
<p>Wiberg won the combined event, which coupled Sunday's slalom with Saturday's downhill.</p>
<p>German Hilde Gerg finished second in the combined and Austria's Anita Wachter was third.</p>
</text>
